The Dudley Heights Project & Financial Realities



Ghee serves as the sole director and ultimate owner of Sanctum Projects, the vehicle behind the 19-unit luxury Dudley Heights townhouse development on Dudley Road. The company secured fast-track approvals for its eastern bays projects under Covid-19 recovery legislation. [1, 2, 3]
However, liquidity issues arose due to construction delays at Dudley Heights. In mid-2024, Sanctum Projects accumulated roughly $3.5 million in debt across 92 unsecured trade creditors, including local builders, building suppliers, professional service firms, and the Environmental Protection Authority (EPA). [1, 2]
Ghee presented subcontractors with a highly publicised "creditor's compromise," famously telling tradies to accept 15 cents on the dollar or receive nothing if the company went into liquidation. Though many out-of-pocket contractors felt "bullied" into voting for the massive 85% haircut to salvage something, the fallout left local subbies deeply angry—a situation worsened when initial payout instalments were delayed. [1, 2, 3]

